(VAR-05: every declarable type is claimed to support two equivalent forms,
 both routed through the same type resolver. For the types that have both,
 the initialized form and the default form really do produce the same kind
 of variable. `timer` has only the default form and `file`/`time` have only
 the initialized form, so the "every" in the claim does not hold — see
 Discrepancy 8.
